## VERIFICATION GAP (next session's first job)
crash_consistency 32/caw PASSED 88s on .482 — but it does NOT exercise
foreign replay: the guest-side script is drop-caches cold-read only (see
header comment "a true node-KILL needs host-side orchestration"). run.sh's
DESTRUCTIVE label/comment (line 337) is historical. The P227-FR-ATOMIC-SKIP
+ P163-RECOVERY-COMPLETE lines on test13 dmesg (slot 30, ts~9239) are from
the PREVIOUS build era = the old publish-after-skip defect signature.
So: to verify the new gate, must kill a node holding committed NON-snlocal
txns (multi-node-active victim → no kind-17/snlocal authorization →
atomic-skip → NEW refusal). Candidates: tests/diag_fence_visibility.sh
(virsh destroys a victim), or fence_during_write, or a targeted repro:
write from victim under shared-dir contention (so txns touch other nodes'
AGs / not snlocal), virsh destroy it, watch elected survivor dmesg for
P227-FR-TORN-UNPUBLISHED + "NOT auto-retried" + NO P163-RECOVERY-COMPLETE
for that slot + no 30s alert storm. Note: if the victim's txns ARE snlocal
(kind-17 accept), replay publishes legitimately — that's the sess187/188
authorized path, not a gate failure; the gate only fires on skips>0.

